{
  "embeddedAssets": {
    "assets": [
      {
        "dataBase64": "",
        "id": "sample.sprite-water-reflection.locked_sprite_texture",
        "mime": "image/png",
        "name": "slime.png"
      }
    ],
    "bindings": {
      "locked_sprite_texture": "sample.sprite-water-reflection.locked_sprite_texture"
    }
  },
  "format": "kshader",
  "generator": "Kekenik Shader",
  "graph": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_inputs",
        "position": {
          "x": 22,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 542
        },
        "text": "Sprite UV and time."
      },
      {
        "color": "#22d3ee",
        "id": "note_depth",
        "position": {
          "x": 768,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 1154
        },
        "text": "`depth = waterline − v` (positive under water). The mirror image is read at `v' = depth / (1 − waterline)`, i.e. the same distance above the line, in the sprite's own 0…1 space. `above = step(waterline, v)` selects the sprite half."
      },
      {
        "color": "#4ade80",
        "id": "note_ripple",
        "position": {
          "x": 2126,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2990
        },
        "text": "`dx = (sin(depth·f − t·speed) + 0.5·sin(depth·1.7f − 1.3·t·speed)) · amount · saturate(depth·4)`: two sines of different frequency don't look periodic, and the `saturate(depth·4)` ramp keeps the reflection attached to the sprite's feet at the waterline."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fb923c",
        "id": "note_sample",
        "position": {
          "x": 5320,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 2072
        },
        "text": "Two **Sprite Texture** reads (*Outside: transparent* so rippled UVs that leave the sprite are empty): the sprite at `(u, (v − waterline) / (1 − waterline))` and the reflection at the rippled mirror UV. Reflection alpha = `a × opacity × (1 − depth / fade)²`; colour = `rgb × water tint`. `lerp(…, above)` picks the half."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fbbf24",
        "id": "note_line",
        "position": {
          "x": 7596,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2072
        },
        "text": "`line = 1 − smoothstep(0, width, |v − waterline|)`: a thin HDR highlight on the surface that also covers the seam between sprite and reflection."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_out",
        "position": {
          "x": 9872,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 300
        },
        "text": "Sprite / reflection colour with the surface line, and the matching alpha."
      }
    ],
